# AGENTS.md

## Response Style

- Concise and direct.
- No unnecessary pleasantries, filler, or unsolicited summaries. Ask clarifying questions only when necessary to confirm objectives or choose between consequential outcomes.
- Keep explanations of code changes to 1 line or fewer; provide rationale only when asked.

## Conventional Commits

Format: `<type>: <description>`. Scope is optional (`feat(auth): add login endpoint`).

type: `feat` new feature / `fix` bug fix / `refactor` refactoring without behavior change / `docs` documentation only / `test` test changes / `chore` maintenance / `perf` performance / `ci` CI/CD

- Lowercase type and description; subject within 72 characters
- Use imperative mood ("add feature", not "added feature")
- 1 commit per logical change

## MCP Tools

In code mode, MCP tools do not appear in the standard tool listing. Invoke them from the `exec` JS sandbox using `tools.mcp__<server>__<tool>`.

- If unsure of available tool names, inspect via `Object.keys(tools)` in `exec`. Never claim "MCP is unavailable" simply because tools do not appear in the default tool list.

## Chezmoi

- When modifying files under `~/.config`, never edit them directly; edit the corresponding source under `~/.local/share/chezmoi/`.
- Run `chezmoi diff` before editing. If uncommitted changes overlap with current tasks, halt and confirm with user.
- Never execute `chezmoi apply` without explicit user permission.

## Communication and Decision Gates

- State objective and conclusion first, followed by rationale, constraints, and steps.
- Define internal terminology and acronyms in a single sentence at first occurrence.
- Explicitly distinguish `Verified Facts`, `Constraints`, `Proposals`, and `Unconfirmed Items`. Never treat proposals as decided.
- Never interpret recommendations, urgency, silence, or implicit consent as approval for design choices or external operations.
- If an undecided choice exists and guessing alters behavior, external impact, or reversibility, present options with impact and risk, asking exactly one question. Halt design changes, child agent launches, external endpoint calls, applies, commits, or deletions until answered.
- When child agents ask questions, forward questions, options, and reasons to user verbatim; parent must not choose on their behalf.
- Before tools or external actions, state once: `What to do / Why needed / What changes / What does not change`.
- In progress updates, state current phase, blockers, changes made, and next decision maker.
- In completion reports, separate completed, verified, unverified, open items, modified files, and commits.

